  "lines": {
   "01-contracts.md:7": "Named ordered immutable observations (JSON/media descriptors), named decision questions, recursively typed output contracts, and explicit execution policy. Output family: Boolean, choice, ranking, pointer, extractive/generated spans and recursively structured compositions. Abstain != False; partial/incomplete/refused/invalid/unsupported/stale are not silently coerced to a choice.",
   "01-contracts.md:11": "The pure compiler validates identifiers, bounded state, digests, RFC 6901 pointer candidates, cardinality, candidate IDs, schema, modality, output bounds, score requirements, distinct axes for thinking, generated spans, extractive spans and read-only observations. Route only after hard capability eligibility and context budgeting. Unknown hard capability = reject. No unrequested summarization or weakening.",
   "02-implementation.md:15": "RI-DEC-07: strict result validator, abstention, atomic/partial batch semantics, retry/cancellation, transient errors and snapshot freshness.",
   "03-conformance.md:14": "Booleans/abstention, rankings/ties/top_k, exact pointer revision/digest checks, Unicode byte/character extractive span offsets, recursively nested structured values, malformed provider tool output, lack of stream-tool semantics, native/generative parity for eligible finalizers, timeout and cancellation, failed atomic joint retry, partial independent result policy, full/partial/missing score provenance, multimodal and context budgets, prompt/template injection scope for declared read-only observations."
  },
